## Rules for every agent

1. Never change files in `System/` without showing the user the change (a plain summary is enough; show the exact text when asked) and getting a yes. Make setup changes with the setup commands in `System/Core/Manual/setup.md`, not by editing files by hand. The only exceptions: saving the user's own name, role and company with `.bron/bin/bron settings set` straight away when they tell you, and saving or forgetting memory (below), which you do straight away without asking first, even though memory files are in `System/`.
2. Never edit `System/Core/`, `.claude/`, `.codex/`, `.agents/`, `AGENTS.md` or `CLAUDE.md`. Bron regenerates them from `System/`.
3. Team members never run as subagents. To hand work to a team member, use a ticket. Subagents are only for helpers.
4. Keep the vault tidy: one-off work in `Projects/`, repeating work in `Routines/`. Machine data lives in `.bron/`.
5. Ask before anything that leaves the vault (sending, sharing, posting, pushing) unless the user chose "always allow" for it.

## Tickets

Work between agents goes through tickets in `Tickets/` (see `System/Core/Manual/tickets.md`).
- Hand work to a team member only when it needs their connections, their model or work they own (their projects and routines). Anything else, do yourself.
- Quick question or short task for a team member: run `.bron/bin/bron ticket new --to <Agent> --from <your name> --title '<short title>' --request '<what to do>' [--context '<what they need to know>'] --run --caller-cli <claude|codex>` as an ordinary command and wait (it takes about 10–20 seconds). When you pass on the user's question, use their own words: don't add tasks, sources or checks they didn't ask for. When it prints the Result, give the user the answer first, then close it with `.bron/bin/bron ticket status <id> done --as <your key>`. For longer work, questions back, approvals or anything that doesn't go to plan, use the delegate skill.
- When the message trigger says a tagged agent (`@name`) is answering, don't answer for them: wait with `.bron/bin/bron ticket wait <id>` and show their reply word for word.
- When you were started to work a ticket, your final reply becomes its Result; just answer. To stop and ask a question, run `.bron/bin/bron ticket status <id> blocked --as <your key> --note '<question>'` (if the text contains a single quote, write it to a file and use `--file` (result) or `--note-file` (status)). Your ticket id is in the task you were given (also in $$BRON_TICKET); your key is your agent name in lower case with hyphens (e.g. cfo).
- If an action is refused or needs approval, don't work around it: mark the ticket blocked with a note starting "Needs your OK:" that names the exact action.

## Memory

Facts you remember are in `System/Memory/Facts.md` (shared) and `System/Agents/<you>/Memory/Facts.md` (yours); summaries of past conversations are in `System/Agents/<you>/Memory/Conversations/`. Your key is your agent name in lower case with hyphens.
- When the user states a lasting preference, decision or fact, or corrects you, save it straight away (no need to ask first: saving memory is the exception to rule 1) with `.bron/bin/bron memory remember '<fact>' --as <your key> [--mine] [--section about-you|firm|decisions|how] [--replaces '<words of the old fact>']` and tell them in one line: "Noted: …". Shared (the default) is for facts about the user, the firm and decisions every agent follows; `--mine` is for how you do your own work. If it contradicts a saved fact, use `--replaces`. If the fact contains a single quote, write it to a file and use `--file <file>` instead of '<fact>'.
- "Forget that" / "that's wrong": straight away, without asking first, run `.bron/bin/bron memory forget '<words>' --as <your key>` (or `--conversation '<title or date>'`), then save the correction if they gave one.
- When the user refers to something from before ("last time", "what did we decide"), run `.bron/bin/bron memory search '<words>' --as <your key>` before asking them; add `--all` to include other agents' conversations.
- When memory is getting long, offer to tidy: draft the cleaned facts file, show it with `.bron/bin/bron memory tidy --as <your key> [--mine] --file <draft> --preview` (the preview names the file it replaces), and apply it (same command without `--preview`) after a yes.
- Never save passwords, keys, tokens, account numbers or sensitive personal details about other people.

